// The marks a package writes to say what its declarations mean to the
// compiler.
//
// The vocabulary is public, and deliberately not in the `internal/` tier: a
// plugin living outside this repository writes the same marks its in-tree
// siblings do. `#[foreign]` records what a declaration corresponds to
// outside SNGL; `#[wildcard]` says what a name nobody declared resolves to; and
// `#[construct]` says a prop is read only while its instance is being built.
//
// The per-target packages under it -- `sngl:platform/html`, `sngl:language/go`
// -- are separate packages, and hold no marks.
